# `distinct *` takes no other columns (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
T | distinct *, a
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..18
  PIPELINE@0..17
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "T"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    DISTINCT_OP@4..17
      IDENT@4..12 "distinct"
      WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
      STAR@13..14 "*"
      COMMA@14..15 ","
      WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
      NAME_REF@16..17
        IDENT@16..17 "a"
  WHITESPACE@17..18 "\n"

error[DS0116]: `distinct *` cannot list other columns
  --> query:1:14
  |
1 | T | distinct *, a
  |              ^ `*` already means every column
  |
  = help: remove `*` to keep the distinct values of the listed columns, or remove the columns to keep distinct rows
